क|कं|कः
1 क॑ stem of the interr. pron. (n. क॑द् older than कि॑म्<BR>q.v.) who, what, which? Used as subst. or adj. in direct & indirect<BR>questions, often connected w. इव, उ, नाम, नु, वा, स्विद्, also w. a<BR>demonstr. pron., e.g. को ऽ यमायाति who comes here? किमिदं कुरुषे<BR>what are you doing there? Used also as indef. pron. = some, any,<BR>whoever, whatever, whichever, esp. after य & मा, before च, चन,<BR>चिद्, & (later) अपि;<BR> कश्च, कश्चन, etc. w. neg. = nobody, none, n.<BR>nothing. कश्चित्-कश्चित् the one—the other;<BR> pl. some-others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
