कनकशक्ति|कनकशक्तिः
कनकशक्ति m. E. of Skanda (lit. Gold-spear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकसूत्र
कनकसूत्र n. a gold cord or chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाब्ज
कनकाब्ज n. gold-lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकोज्ज्वल
कनकोज्ज्वल a. shining with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनखल|कनखलं
कनखल n. N. of a bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कना
कना॑ f. a girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्क|कनिष्कः
कनिष्क m. N. of an Indo-Scythic^1 king.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ॑ (superl.) the smallest, least, lowest,<BR>youngest, younger;<BR> f. आ the youngest wife, (±अन्गुलि) the little<BR>finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
क॑निष्ठ (superl.) the smallest, least, lowest,<BR>youngest, younger;<BR> f. आ the youngest wife, (±अन्गुलि) the little<BR>finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठक|कनिष्ठकं
कनिष्ठक^1 f. ˚ष्ठिका॑ the smallest;<BR> f. कनि॑ष्ठिका<BR>the little finger;<BR> subordination, obedience.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160315. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनी
