कल्प|कल्पः
क॑ल्प a. feasible, possible;<BR> fit for, able to, capable of<BR>(gen., loc., inf., or —˚). m. ordinance, rule, esp. for ceremonial or<BR>sacrificial acts, practise, custom, manner, way (adj. —˚ having the<BR>manner or way of —. i.e. resembling —, similar to —;<BR> after an adj.<BR>almost, as it were);<BR> a fabulous period of time, a day of Brahman or 1000<BR>yugas. एतेन कल्पेन in this way. प्रथमः कल्पः or<BR>प्रथमकल्पः primary rule (opp. अनुकल्प), chief matter, main<BR>point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

