तार|तारं|तारः
तार॑ a. all-pervading, esp. of a sound, i.e. loud, high,<BR>shrill;<BR> or of light, i.e. shining, radiant. — m. passing over, crossing<BR>(only —˚);<BR> saver, deliverer (E. of sev. gods), a clear or beautiful<BR>pearl, a man's name. f. आ a star or meteor, the pupil of the eye;<BR> N.<BR>of sev. goddesses & women. n. descent to a river, bank;<BR> a loud or shrill<BR>sound (also m.);<BR> तारम् as adv. aloud;<BR> comp. तारतरम्, superl.<BR>तारतमम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक|तारकं|तारकः
तारक (f. ˚रिका) carrying over, rescuing;<BR> m. N. of a<BR>demon, pl. the children of T.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=202" target="_blank">Page202</a>]<BR>f. ता॑रका star (also n.),<BR>meteor, pupil of the eye, a woman's name;<BR> f. तारिका the juice of<BR>palms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

