तावन्त्|तावत्
ता॑वन्त् a. so great, so much (many), so long, so far<BR>(correl. w. या॑वन्त् q.v.). n. तावत् adv. so much, so long, so far;<BR>for a while, in the mean time (also instr. or loc.);<BR> first, at once,<BR>just, now (esp. w. imperat. or 1. pers. pres. or fut.);<BR> indeed, of<BR>course, it is true, one must admit. Often only emphasizing (±एव). —<BR>न तावत् not yet,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=203" target="_blank">Page203</a>]<BR>not at all, मा तावत् by no means!<BR>तावत्-यावत् (±न) as long or as far—as. या॑वद्यावत् —<BR>ता॑वत्तावत् gradually as — (so). तावत् — च no sooner-than.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

