त्वेष॑नृम्ण a. of impetuous courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषप्रतीक
त्वेष॑प्रतीक a. of brilliant appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषयाम
त्वेष॑याम a. of impetuous course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषस्
त्वेष॑स् n. vehemence, energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेषसंदृश्
त्वेष॑संदृश् a. of brilliant aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वेष्य
त्वेष्य॑ a. shaking, agitating, awful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वोत
त्वो॑त a. helped or protected by thee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वोति
त्वो॑ति a. enjoying thy help or favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सर्
त्सर् त्स॑रति creep, sneak, steal upon. अभि & उप = S.<BR>अव sneak away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरा
त्सरा f. stealing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्स॑रु m. a creeping animal;<BR> stalk of a leaf;<BR> hilt or handle<BR>of a sword, poss. ˚मन्त्†.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सारिन्
त्सारि॑न् a. creeping, stealing near;<BR> crooked, hidden,<BR>secret.<BR>!!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थरथराय्
थरथराय् थरथरा˚यते reel, stagger, shake,<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थूर्व्
थूर्व् only pp. थू॑र्वन्त् E. of Agni.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">Page216</a>]<BR>!!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
1 द (—˚) giving, granting, causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
2 द (—˚) cutting off, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्
दंश् द॑शति (द॑श˚ते & दंशति), pp. दष्ट॑ r.<BR>दंशित (q.v.) bite. C. दंशयति cause a pers. (acc.) to be bitten<BR>by (instr.). —निस्, परि & वि bite through. सम् bite, seize with the<BR>teeth, press together. — Cf. संदष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश m. biting, a bite or the spot bitten;<BR> gadfly;<BR> armour,<BR>mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशच्छेद
दंशच्छेद m. the cutting out of a bitten spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन n. biting;<BR> armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशमशक
दंशमशक n. sgl. gadflies and gnats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित a. bitten, stung;<BR> mailed, armed;<BR> prepared, ready<BR>for (loc.);<BR> pressed together, crowded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशुक
दं॑शुक a. biting (acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश्मन्
दंश्मन् n. a bite or the place bitten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्टृ
दंष्टृ॑ m. biter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्र
दं॑ष्ट्र m. दंष्ट्रा f. large tooth, tusk, fang.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्राकराल
दंष्ट्राकराल a. having terrible tusks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रायुध|दंष्ट्रायुधः
दंष्ट्रायुध a. having tusks as weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन् a. tusked;<BR> m. beast of prey or snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंस्
दंस् (only दंस॑यस्) possess wonderful power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसन|दंसनं
दंस॑न n. marvellous power or deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसना
दंस॑ना f. the same;<BR> poss. ˚वन्त्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसस्
दं॑सस् n. = prec. f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसिष्ठ
दं॑सिष्ठ superl. to seq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसु
दं॑सु a. wonderfully strong (˚—);<BR> n. adv. wonderfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसुपत्नी
दं॑सुपत्नी f. having a powerful lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष्
दक्ष् द॑क्षति द॑क्ष˚ते A. satisfy, please (dat.);<BR> M.<BR>be able or strong. C. दक्ष॑यति make able or strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
द॑क्ष a. able, capable, appropriate, suitable, fit for,<BR>clever in (loc. or —˚);<BR> strong, mighty;<BR> intelligent, wise, right (not<BR>left). m. ability, power, fitness, cleverness, intelligence, energy,<BR>will, disposition, (evil) design;<BR> N. of an Aditya, also identif. w.<BR>Prajāpati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षकन्या
द॑क्षकन्या f. Dakṣa's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षक्रतु
1 दक्षक्रतु॑ m. du. will and intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षक्रतु
2 द॑क्षक्रतु a. having a strong intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षत्
द॑क्षत् a. gleaming, glittering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षता
दक्षता f. ability, dexterity, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षपितृ
द॑क्षपितृ a. having Dakṣa as father or gifted with<BR>cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षस्
द॑क्षस् a. able, strong, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसुत|दक्षसुतः
दक्षसुत m. आ f. son & daughter of Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षा॑य्य a. to be obeyed or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
द॑क्षिण a. able, capable of, fit for (—˚);<BR> right (not<BR>left), southern;<BR> upright, honest;<BR> amiable, polite, chivalrous.<BR>दक्षिणं w. परि-इ walk round a person with the right side towards<BR>him;<BR> w. कृ = दक्षिणतःकृ q.v. —m. the right hand or arm, the right<BR>hand horse;<BR> the right side, the south (m. or n.). f. आ (scil. गो) a<BR>good milch-cow;<BR> a present given to officiating priests (orig. a cow);<BR>fee, donation, gift i.g.;<BR> (±दिश्) the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण॑ a. able, capable of, fit for (—˚);<BR> right (not<BR>left), southern;<BR> upright, honest;<BR> amiable, polite, chivalrous.<BR>दक्षिणं w. परि-इ walk round a person with the right side towards<BR>him;<BR> w. कृ = दक्षिणतःकृ q.v. —m. the right hand or arm, the right<BR>hand horse;<BR> the right side, the south (m. or n.). f. आ (scil. गो) a<BR>good milch-cow;<BR> a present given to officiating priests (orig. a cow);<BR>fee, donation, gift i.g.;<BR> (±दिश्) the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतस्
दक्षिणत॑स् adv. from the right or the south;<BR> on the<BR>right side or south of (gen.). With कृ turn the right to a person (as<BR>a mark of esteem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणत्रा
दक्षिणत्रा॑ adv. on the right side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणत्व
दक्षिणत्व n. honesty, amiableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपवन
दक्षिणपवन m. the south-wind^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपश्चिम
दक्षिणपश्चिम a. south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्व
दक्षिणपूर्व a. south-eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणा
दक्षिणा॑ adv. on the right or on the south of (abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्
दक्षिणात् (abl. adv.) from or on the right or south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणापथ m. the Dekhan (lit. southern path or<BR>country).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापर
दक्षिणापर a. south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रत्यञ्च्
दक्षिणाप्रत्यञ्च् f. ˚तीची south-western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणा॑प्रवण a. sloping to the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाभिमुख
दक्षिणाभिमुख a. facing or flowing southwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणामुख|दक्षिणामुखः
दक्षिणामुख a. turning the face to the right or to<BR>the south;<BR> n. adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायन|दक्षिणायनं
दक्षिणायन n. the southern progress (of the sun), the<BR>summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणारण्य
दक्षिणारण्य n. the southern forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावन्त्|दक्षिणावत्
द॑क्षिणावन्त् a. able, fit;<BR> rich in offerings or<BR>presents, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः|दक्षिणावर्त्त
दक्षिणावर्त m. = दक्षिणापथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशिरस्
दक्षिणाशिरस् a. turning the head towards the south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावृत्
दक्षिणावृ॑त् a. turned or going round towards the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाहि
*दक्षिणाहि adv. far on the right or in the south of<BR>(abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीकृ
दक्षिणी@कृ = दक्षिणं@कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणी॑य a. worthy of the sacrificial fee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

