नामन्
ना॑मन् n. (adj. —˚ f. नाम्नी, r. नामन्) name,<BR>appellation, esp. personal name (opp. गोत्र);<BR> characteristic form,<BR>nature, species;<BR> noun (g.). ना॑म्ना or नाम (also both together or w.<BR>नामतस्) by name, called. — ना॑म ग्रभ् (ग्रह्) call or address by<BR>name, mention (gen.);<BR> नाम भृ bear a name, be called, नाम कृ, दा,<BR>or धा give a name,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=267" target="_blank">Page267</a>]<BR>call;<BR> नाम्ना कृ or विधा call, term (2<BR>acc.). Acc. नाम also adv. namely, indeed, of course;<BR> perhaps,<BR>probably, indeed, then (esp. after an interr. pron.). अपि नाम I<BR>wonder if, perhaps, मा नाम would that not —, if only not (opt.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

