परलोकहस्त
परलोकहस्त a. sure of (lit. holding in the hand)<BR>the future world.*<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवत्ता
परवत्ता f. abstr. to seq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवन्त्|परवत्
परवन्त् a. subject to another, powerless, helpless,<BR>beside one's self;<BR> dependent on, devoted to (loc., gen., or —˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश|परवशः
परवश a. subject to another's wish, dependent on<BR>another;<BR> mastered or ruled by (—˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवारण
परवारण m. chaser of foes.*<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवीरहन्
परवीरहन् a. killing hostile heroes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशु|परशुः
परशु॑ m. hatchet, axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुमन्त्|परशुमत्
परशुम॑न्त् a. poss. to prec.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुराम|परशुरामः
परशुराम m. E. of Rama (R. with the axe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वध|परश्वधः
परश्वध m. hatchet, axe;<BR> p. ˚धिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वस्
परश्वस् adv. the day after to-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परःशत॑ a. pl. more than a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्
पर॑स् adv. beyond, on the other or opposite side, (as prep.<BR>w. acc., instr., or abl.);<BR> further, later, afterwards, in future;<BR>without, except (instr. or abl.);<BR> above, more than (acc., instr., or ˚—<BR>in numerals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तरम्
परस्तर॑म् adv. farther away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तराम्
परस्˚तरा॑म् adv. farther away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तात्
पर॑स्तात् adv. & prep. (w. gen.) beyond, on the other<BR>side, below or above, in future, later, after;<BR> afterwards, towards or<BR>away;<BR> from above, before, or behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्थान
परस्थान n. foreign place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्प
पर॑स्प protecting;<BR> n. = seq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पत्व
परस्पत्व॑ n. protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पर|परस्परं
परस्पर (only the obl. cases of m. sgl., n. & ˚—<BR>adv.) each other, one another, mutual(ly)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परतस्
परस्परतस् adv. = abl. to prec.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परादिन्
परस्परादिन् a. eating each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पा
परस्पा॑ m. protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्मैपद|परस्मैपदं
परस्मैपद n. the form for another, i.e. the active<BR>or transitive form of the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्व
परस्व n. another's property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वन्त्|परस्वत्
प॑रस्वन्त् m. the wild ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वादायिन्
परस्वादायिन् a. seizing another's property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
प॑रःसहस्र a. more than a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परःसहस्र॑ a. more than a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परा
प॑रा adv. (only ˚— in subst. & verbs) away, off, forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक|पराकः
पराक॑ s. distance (only loc. & abl.);<BR> m. a kind of<BR>penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकात्तात्
पराका॑त्तात् adv. from afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रम|पराक्रमः
पराक्रम m. sgl. & pl. bold advance, courage, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग|परागः
पराग m. sgl. & pl. the pollen of a flower (poss. ˚गिन्),<BR>dust i.g.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागम|परागमः
परागम m. the arrival or attack of an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग्वदन
पराग्वदन a. = पराङ्मुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग्वदनशालिन्
पराग्˚वदनशालिन् a. = पराङ्मुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्ग|परांग
पराङ्ग n. the hinder part of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मनस्
प॑राङ्मनस् a. having the mind directed backwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुख|पराङ्मुखः
पराङ्मुख f. ई a. having the face turned backwards,<BR>averted, turned away;<BR> flying from, avoiding, shunning, not caring for<BR>(abl., loc., gen., प्रति w. acc., or —˚);<BR> contrary, unfavourable.<BR>—n. adv., abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखीकृ
परान्मुखी@कृ put to flight;<BR> w. भू take to flight,<BR>turn the back upon (gen.), be contrary or unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीन|पराचीनः
पराची॑न a. turned away, averted, opposite;<BR> not caring<BR>for, indifferent about (abl.);<BR> n. adv. beyond, away, after (as prep. w.<BR>abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचैस्
पराचै॑स् adv. away, aside, off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजय|पराजयः
पराजय m. conquest, victory (gen. or —˚);<BR> defeat,<BR>deprivation, loss (abl. or —˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजित|पराजितः
प॑राजित a. conquered, overthrown;<BR> having lost (a<BR>lawsuit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजिष्णु
†पराजिष्णु a. succumbent or victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्च्|परांच्
प॑राञ्च् (f. प॑राची, n. पराक् & परान्) directed away,<BR>averted, opposite to, turning from (abl.), behind or after one another,<BR>following upon (abl.);<BR> departed, lost;<BR> turned outwards (the organs of<BR>sense);<BR> n. adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परातरम्
परातर॑म् adv. further away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्मन्
परात्मन् m. the supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराददि
पराददि॑ a. giving up, delivering (acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादान|परादानं
परादा॑न n. the action of giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीन|पराधीनः
पराधीन a. subject to another, dependent or intent<BR>upon, occupied with (—˚);<BR> abstr. ˚ता f.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परानीक
परानीक n. hostile troop.*<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परानुदे
परानु॑दे (dat. inf.) to push away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्त|परांत|परान्तः
परान्त m. the final end, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापर|परापरं|परापरः
परापर n. the far and near, more and less, better and<BR>worse, earlier and later, cause and effect;<BR> abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभव|पराभवः
पराभव॑ m. going away, parting, vanishing,<BR>disappearance, also = seq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभाव|पराभावः
पराभाव m. defeat, humiliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभूति|पराभूतिः
प॑राभूति f. = prec.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्श|परामर्शः
परामर्श m. seizure, touch;<BR> attack, injury loc., gen.,<BR>or —˚);<BR> relation, insinuation, recollection, reflection, consideration,<BR>thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायण|परायणं
परा॑यण n. going away, departure, last way or exit;<BR>final end or aim, last resort or refuge;<BR> essence, sum, chief matter;<BR> N.<BR>of a work. —˚ having a thing as highest object or occupation, i.e.<BR>quite filled with, devoted to, or intent upon (cf. प॑र). — Adj.<BR>violent, strong, being the last refuge or essential matter of, conducive<BR>to, dependent on (gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायत्त|परायत्तं
परायत्त a. dependent on, subject to (—˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
1 परार्थ m. highest (or another's) advantage, interest,<BR>business, or matter. ˚—, acc. & loc. adv. for another's sake, for<BR>others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
2 परार्थ a. having another object, dependent on another<BR>person or thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थवादिन्
परार्थवादिन्^1 a. speaking for another,<BR>representative (j.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160418. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/289. note: cf ccs, mw, pw, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्ध
परार्ध॑ m. the other or more remote side or half;<BR> the<BR>highest number (also n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्ध्य
परार्ध्य a. being on the other or more remote side or<BR>half;<BR> finest, best, most excellent;<BR> more excellent than (abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावत्|परावन्त्
पराव॑त् f. distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर
परावर n. = परापर;<BR> also adj. more distant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">Page299</a>]<BR>and nearer, higher and lower, all-including;<BR> m. pl. ancestors and<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृज्
परावृ॑ज् m. outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशर|पराशरः
पराशर॑ m. destroyer, a man's name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रय|पराश्रयः
1 पराश्रय m. dependence on others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रय|पराश्रयः
2 पराश्रय a. dependent on others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासु|परासुः
परासु a. dying or dead (lit. whose breath is going or gone<BR>out).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासेध|परासेधः
परासेध m. arrest, prison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्य
परा॑स्य a. to be cast away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्य
परास्य॑ a. to be cast away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह्ण|पराह्णः
पराह्ण m. the afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
प॑रि adv. round, about (often ˚—, also to denote abundance<BR>or high degree);<BR> prep. round, about, against, opposite to, beyond,<BR>above, more than (acc.);<BR> from, out of, after, in consequence or on<BR>account of, according to (abl.);<BR> *around i.e. outside or with exception<BR>of (abl., also परि परि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर|परिकरः
परिकर m. attendance, assistance, followers, servants,<BR>troop, multitude (also pl.);<BR> a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

