पाद|पादः
पा॑द m. foot, leg (lit. & fig.), foot as a measure;<BR> column,<BR>pillar;<BR> ray, beam (as the foot of a heavenly body);<BR> fourth part, quarter<BR>of anything, esp. of a four-versed stanza, also part or verse i.g.,<BR>section, chapter. Often pl. the feet of (—˚) i.e. the venerable —.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

