पू॑र्व a. being before (sp. & t.), fore, first, eastern, to<BR>the east of (abl.);<BR> prior, preceding, ancient, previous to, earlier than<BR>(abl. or —˚, often ˚— or —˚ w. pp. in the sense of an adv., e.g.<BR>पूर्वोक्त or उक्तपूर्व spoken before or already);<BR> accompanied by,<BR>following;<BR> with, under, according to (—˚);<BR> w. वयस् n. youth;<BR> w.<BR>आयुस् n. old age. —m. elder brother, pl. the ancestors or ancients. f.<BR>पूर्वा (±दिश्) the east. n. forepart, as adv. in front, before (as<BR>prep. w. abl.), first, previously, already, long since;<BR> —˚ accompanied<BR>by etc. (cf. adj. —˚). पूर्व उत्तर former-latter, n. adv.<BR>first-last;<BR> अद्य पूर्वम् until now, hitherto.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्वक|पूर्वकः|पूर्व्वक
पूर्वक f. पूर्विका earlier^1, former, previous;<BR> —˚ adj. &<BR>n. adv. accompanied by etc. = prec.;<BR> m. ancestor, forefather.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

