ब्रह्मद्विष्
ब्रह्मद्वि॑ष् a. hating devotion or the Brahmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मद्वेष|ब्रह्मद्वेषः
ब्रह्मद्वेष m. hatred of devotion, impiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
1 ब्र॑ह्मन् n. devotion (lit. swelling, sc. of the soul),<BR>worship, piety, holy life, chastity;<BR> hymn of praise, prayer;<BR> sacred<BR>text, magic formula, incantation, the syllable Om, the Veda, i.g. divine<BR>science, theology or theosophy;<BR> the priestly or sacerdotal class;<BR> the<BR>supreme Being regarded as impersonal, the Absolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
2 ब्रह्म॑न् m. one who prays, any devout person or a priest;<BR>a knower of sacred knowledge, a Brahman of caste or the priest so<BR>called;<BR> the supreme Being, personif. as the highest god or creator of<BR>the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

