मनस्
म॑नस् n. mind, soul, heart;<BR> the internal organ of<BR>perception and cognition (ph.);<BR> intellect,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=395" target="_blank">Page395</a>]<BR>reason, thought;<BR>excogitation, invention;<BR> wish, inclination, desire, endeavour;<BR>sentiment, disposition;<BR> adj. —˚ wishing or intending to (esp. w. an<BR>infin. in तु). — Instr. म॑नसा in the mind, in thought;<BR> with the<BR>heart, willingly. मनः कृ take to (gen.);<BR> determine, resolve;<BR> also =<BR>˚ धा, विधा, बन्ध्, etc. direct the mind towards, think of (loc.,<BR>dat., acc. w. प्रति, or infin.);<BR> मनसि कृ or निधा take to heart,<BR>consider, imagine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

