योग्य|योग्यं|योग्यः
यो॑ग्य a. fit for the yoke, i.g. fit, suitable, useful,<BR>conducive to, qualified for, capable of (gen., loc., dat., infin., or<BR>—˚). m. beast for draught;<BR> f. योग्या॑ setting to work, preparation,<BR>contrivance, practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्यता
योग्यता f. ˚त्व n. abstr. to prec. adj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजक
योजक m. harnesser, employer (—˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
