रब्धा
रब्धा f. food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ्
रभ् रम्भ्, र॑भते, र॑भ˚ति (रम्भ्ति, ˚ते), pp. रब्ध<BR> (—˚ w. act. & pass. mg) take hold, seize, embrace. C. रम्भयमि &<BR>D. रिप्सते (only —˚). — अनु grasp, seize. आ take hold upon,<BR>touch, seize, lean or stay upon (acc.), reach to, attain;<BR> undertake,<BR>begin to (acc. or infin.). अन्वा take hold of from behind, hold on to<BR>(acc.). समन्वा take hold of each other or together. अभ्या grasp,<BR>touch, get at, undertake, begin. प्रा & समा the same. परि &<BR>संपरि embrace (together). सम् take hold of (each other), seize<BR>upon, partake of, enjoy (instr.);<BR> M. P. be excited or agitated.<BR>अभिसम् grasp, hold fast. — Cf. आ॑रब्ध (sic!), आरभ्य,<BR>प्रारब्ध, स॑रब्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ
रभ m. N. of a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस्
र॑भस् n. impetuosity, fierceness, violence;<BR> instr. adv.<BR>violently, furiously, rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस|रभसः
रभस॑ a. impetuous, fierce, violent, strong. m. = prec.<BR>+ energy, zeal, ardent desire of (—˚);<BR> ˚—, instr., & abl. = prec. adv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस्वन्त्|रभस्वत्
र॑भस्वन्त् a. impetuous, violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभि
र॑भि f. a cert. part of a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभिष्ठ
र॑भिष्ठ (superl.) very impetuous or fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभीयंस्
र॑भीयंस्^1 (compar.) the same.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160418. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/289. note: cf mw (raBIyas), ccs, pw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ्यस्
र॑भ्यस् (compar.) the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभोदा
रभोदा॑ a. giving impetuous strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्
रम् र॑मते र॑म˚ति रम्णाति pp. रते (q.v.) tr.<BR>stop, fix, settle;<BR> gladden, delight, enjoy (esp. carnally);<BR> intr. stop,<BR>rest, stay gladly with (loc. or dat.);<BR> delight in, be pleased with or to<BR>(loc., instr., or infin.);<BR> be happy or content;<BR> dally or have sexual<BR>intercourse with (instr. ±समम्, सह, साकम्, or सार्धम्). C.<BR>रम॑यति or राम॑यति = S. trans. — अनु A. stop (intr.), stay;<BR>M. find pleasure or delight. अभि M. stop, stay;<BR> delight in, be<BR>satisfied or pleased with (loc. or instr. ±सह). उपाव M. feel<BR>comfortable. आ A. stop, cease;<BR> take delight in (loc.), enjoy carnally<BR>(instr. ±समम्). उपा A. (M.) rest, repose, desist from (abl.).<BR>व्युपा & समा the same. उप A. stop (tr.);<BR> A.M. stop (intr.), rest,<BR>stay repose;<BR> cease from, renounce, resign (abl.). व्युप A. M. come to<BR>rest, cease, desist from (abl.). नि M. go to rest, cease, end. C.<BR>निरामयति stop, check, restrain. परि A. take pleasure in, rejoice<BR>at (abl.). वि A. (M.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=444" target="_blank">Page444</a>]<BR>stop, cease, pause, rest;<BR> desist from<BR>(abl.), renounce, resign (abl. or absol.). C. विरमयति or<BR>विरामयति bring to rest or to an end. — Cf. अनुरत, उपरत<BR>(add.), निरत (to be placed after निरञ्जन), विरत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम a. gladdening, delighting (—˚);<BR> f. आ fortune, riches,<BR>splendour, E. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमट
रमट^1 m. pl. N. of a people.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160412. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/275. note: cf. pw = ramaWa (MW).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमटक
रमट˚क^1 m. pl. N. of a people.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160412. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/275. note: ? This not found in other dictionaries. However, since given as an alternate to 'rawa' which is misspelling of 'ramawa', this 'ka' must be added to 'ramawa', hence 'ramawaka'..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण|रमणं|रमणः
