वर|वरं|वरः
2 वर॑ a. choosing ( = ˚);<BR> m. suitor, lover, bridegroom or<BR>the b.'s friend, husband, son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
3 व॑र a. choice, select;<BR> most excellent, fairest, best of<BR>(gen., loc., abl., or —˚);<BR> fairer or better than (abl. or gen.). n.<BR>rather or more than (abl. ±आ॑);<BR> वंर — न (च, तु, पुनर्) (it is)<BR>better — than;<BR> वरं कुर्यात् he had better or he might rather do. m.<BR>(n.) choice, wish, request, boon, gift, reward, privilege, dowry, alms.<BR>—व॑रं वृ, याच्, काङ्ख्, etc. choose a gift or utter a wish, ˚दा॑ or<BR>प्रयम् grant a gift, ˚लभ् have a wish fulfilled^1. व॑रं वरम्,<BR>प्र॑ति व॑रम् & व॑रमा॑ according to wish, at pleasure वरा॑य to<BR>satisfaction, at heart's content.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

