शास्
1 शास् शा॑स्ति शा॑स्ते (शासति शास˚ते) pp. शिष्ट॑<BR>(q.v.), शास्त, & शासित chasten, punish, correct, rule, govern,<BR>manage, direct, instruct, teach, order, command, announce, proclaim,<BR>foretell, avow, confess. — अनु teach, instruct, order, command (2<BR>acc.);<BR> direct, indicate;<BR> rule, govern (±राज्यम् or स्वराज्यम्);<BR>chastise, punish. अभ्यनु indicate, designate. समनु teach, impart<BR>(2 acc.);<BR> w. राज्यम् rule, bear sway. अभि indicate, direct, rule.<BR>आ M.(A.) wish, pray or hope for (acc.);<BR> expect from (abl.);<BR> ±आशि॑षम्<BR>& आशिषस् make supplication, utter wishes for (dat. or loc.). उद्<BR>direct upwards (to the gods). प्र instruct, teach, direct, order,<BR>command;<BR> dispose of, decide (acc. ±अधि);<BR> rule, govern (±राज्यम्).<BR>संप्र w. राज्यम् bear sway, reign. वि give various instructions<BR>about (acc.). सम् direct, bid, invite. — Cf. अ॑नुशिष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

