श्वस्
1 श्वस् श्व॑सिति, श्व॑सति, ˚ते, pp.<BR>श्वस्त & श्वसित (q.v.) blow, bluster, hiss, whistle, snort,<BR>breathe, sigh. I. only शा॑श्वसत् snorting.—अभि blow hither, hiss,<BR>whistle, groan. आ, पर्या, प्रत्या, & समा get breath, recover, become<BR>quiet. C. quiet, comfort. उद् hiss, pant, gasp, groan, sigh;<BR> breathe<BR>upwards or out;<BR> stop or pause from (abl.), recover;<BR> heave (intr.), get<BR>loose, open, expand. C. cause to take breath, refresh, lift up;<BR> tear,<BR>rend asunder, interrupt, disturb. प्रोद pant, breathe heavily. समुद्<BR>take breath, recover;<BR> rise, spring up. C. lift swell (tr.). नि & विनि<BR>hiss, pant, sigh. निस् hiss, pant, breathe out or in, sigh. विनिस्<BR>hiss, pant, snort;<BR> heave a sigh. प्र blow forth or in, exhale or<BR>inhale. C. cause to breathe;<BR> quiet, comfort. अभिप्र blow forth upon<BR>(acc.). वि have confidence, be fearless, trust in (loc., gen., or<BR>acc.). C. inspire confidence (acc.). अतिवि have (too) great confidence<BR>in (loc. or acc.). अभिवि C. inspire confidence. परिवि C. quiet,<BR>comfort. — Cf. उच्छ्वसित, निश्वसित, परिविश्वस्त (add.), विश्वस्त,<BR>समुच्छ्वसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
2 श्व॑स् adv. to-morrow, next day;<BR> श्वः श्वस् from day to day,<BR>daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

