सिद्ध a. hit (aim), attained;<BR> brought about, accomplished,<BR>prepared, ready;<BR> settled, established, known, valid;<BR> resulting,<BR>following;<BR> fallen to one's share, one's own;<BR> peculiar, particular;<BR>perfected^1 or sanctified;<BR> thoroughly skilled in magical arts or endowed<BR>with supernatural powers. m. seer, fortune-teller, a great saint or one<BR>of the blessed (a class of semi-divine beings). n. supernatural power,<BR>magic art.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

