सेव्
सेव् से॑वते (से॑व˚ति), pp. सेवित stay by (acc. or<BR>loc.), inhabit, frequent, visit;<BR> serve, revere, worship;<BR> attend upon,<BR>devote one's self to (acc.);<BR> practise, use, employ, enjoy (also<BR>sexually). C. सेवयति serve, worship. — अनु stay or dwell in;<BR> wait<BR>on, reverence. आ = S. समा devote one's self to (acc.), practise,<BR>use, employ. उप = S. अभ्युप worship, revere. नि (षेवते) stay<BR>in, have intercourse with (loc.);<BR> inhabit, visit, frequent, etc. = S.<BR>परि (षेवते & सेवते) visit, follow, obey, revere;<BR> practise, like.<BR>सम् be together, stay at or with, dwell in, frequent, visit etc. = S.<BR>— Cf. निषेवित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=CAE&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=cae" target="_blank">Correction</a>

